    "placementHash": "sha256:85b7dddedb0b0f72fd789b9bf91d35c4545921d22fa74d1787c5aa090a8b141f",
    "notes": "The Museo Nacional de Antropología PMTiles point, adjoining gallery and entrance footprints, exact roof opening and two water outlines identify the museum associated with Q524249. The entrance faces east toward Chapultepec. The gallery, entrance, canopy and pools use their mapped outlines. Visible roof details, lattice modules, the carved bronze relief and plaza fittings are medium-fi interpretations of ordinary photographs. The localized grade cut compensates for coarse viewer terrain across the pedestrian court. The water curtain is static geometry. Underground circulation and museum exhibits are outside the exterior scope. Physical-device timings are unmeasured."
  },
